THOUGHT: C.3 failures are all slash-command parsing and side effects. I’ll add a `run_slash` core helper and route message creation through it, preserving literal `//` behavior, enforcing `/me` validation, transforming `/shrug`, and returning side-effect envelopes for topic/invite/archive commands.

```mswea_bash_command
cat >> /app/core.py <<'PY'

def run_slash(user,channel,body):
    if body.startswith('//'): return {'body':body[1:]}
    if not body.startswith('/'): return {'body':body}
    parts=body.split(' ',1); cmd=parts[0]; arg=parts[1] if len(parts)>1 else ''
    if cmd=='/me':
        if not arg.strip(): raise ValueError()
        return {'body':body}
    if cmd=='/shrug': return {'body':(arg+' ' if arg else '')+'¯\\_(ツ)_/¯'}
    if cmd in ('/topic','/archive','/unarchive','/invite'):
        return {'side':cmd,'arg':arg}
    raise ValueError()
PY
